d  you're a strange one you're still a  shameless fool so you value something  more than your own pride and quote and  then he agrees to instruct him once  zoro's wounds heal he also thinks to  himself that zorro is a clumsy fool and  when a man of his caliber abandons his  pride it is always for the sake of  another and in this case we can assume  it's for luffy's sake i love this  exchange because again it shows how  confident mihawk is in his own power he  already let zoro live during the barathe  arc so that he could become stronger and  challenge him again but now he's taking  it further and offering to train a much  stronger zorro who wants to defeat him  it's a huge flex on mihawk's part that  he takes zorro on as a student not even  worried about the fact that zoro wants  to defeat him truly legendary behavior  from mihawk so mihawk went on to train  him for two years and taught zoro how to  imbue his source with haki and although  some people claim that zoro may already  be able to beat mihawk i think that the  conversation shouldn't even be on the  table until zorro succeeds in turning  his swords into permanent black blades  as mihawk did during the whole cake  island arc we learned through a cover  story that mihawk was able to get the  monkeys to not only leave him alone as  we know but also to help him till the  old battleground of the former muggy  kingdom another nod to his strength  since he was able to get those  aggressive and wild human drills to  submit to his authority and so we get to  wano country the ark that went a long  way and re-hyping up mihawk after as i  explained he left something to be  desired at marineford especially when  compared to yonko shanks his long-time  rival slash friend after the world  government disbanded the warlord system  the marines came after mihawk asking him  to surrender initially mihawk said he  felt the thrill of excitement again  since it had been so long since he was  chased however despite being strong  enough to not get caught thrill  eventually turned into annoyance and so  comes in cross guild crocodile calls  miak one day despite clashing at  marineford these two clearly have enough  respect for one another to hear each  other out it's at this point that mihawk  tells crocodile the navy has his island  surrounded at the moment and so he needs  to pick up and move base as bothersome  as it may be it's at this point that  crocodile says that's why he should come  over to crocodile side with their  combined names the navy would have to  sit up and take notice crocodile even  points out that hawkeye was known as the  naval hunter aka marine hunter once  which is such a good detail again  although pirate hunter sounds cool  marine hunter is way cooler you'd have  to be insanely strong to get away with  being a solo marine hunter and beyond  that as mentioned it seems like they  couldn't deal with him and so they  offered him the position of warlord to  get him to stop and ironically mihawk  and crocodile find common ground in the  fact that they both have distrust for  others it's telling that crocodile  wanted mihawk to be his partner even  though they've clashed before we also  find out that mihawk's bounty is a  whopping 3.59 billion which is insane  when you consider he's not even a yonko  in fact even though the government  thinks that he's following buggy they  still gave mihawk the bigger bounty  something we've never seen before as far  as i remember furthermore the marines  didn't just call him the strongest  swordsman in the world they also said  that he has greater sword skill than  even shanks and it is at this point that  once again you can start to make the  argument that mihawk is stronger than  shanks as individuals again it's a gray  area and we don't know a lot of details  for certain and shanks has been hyped up  more than mihawk you can't deny that but  it's completely justifiable now to raise  the possibility that mihawk is stronger  think about 