urehead  and mihawk and crocodile are pretty much  the ones in charge and even with that  being said it was miha who made the  executive decision to let buggy be the  face of the organization and crocodile  went along with his decision suggesting  that mihawk the one with the highest  bounty is the one calling the shots when  he wants to and that wraps up everything  we know about mihawk up to this point  and shows how there were moments that  made us question if he could really be  as strong as shanks and there were  moments as well that suggested he's  stronger one-on-one at least however  even mihawk acknowledges that one on one  is not the most dangerous power the most  dangerous power is when people want to  help you as he noticed with luffy and  this was reaffirmed when he decided to  join cross guild rather than continuing  on alone allies are powerful and shanks  always had more but mihawk has started  to surround himself with some as well  and again the only way i can explain the  fact that vista and crocodile were able  to hold back a yonko level character is  by pointing to the fact that fights in  one piece are not like fights in other  series even if the gap is big as i  mentioned with kaido and yamato fights  can still take a while so in that case  it's not all that surprising that  someone who could potentially beat  shanks eventually would get held back by  weaker but not weak characters like  vista and crocodile but let me know your  thoughts have an open mind and tell me  your honest thoughts about the famous  mihawk vs shanks debate the point with  this video was not to give a definitive  answer to something oda has tiptoed  around and yet chosen not to reveal but  to retrace mihawk's steps so that we  have a better idea of his power and to  spark discussion i for my part have to  admit that chapter 1058 definitely  influenced the way i personally view the  mihawk vs shanks debate now channel the  pirate king with it and smash that like  button if